WEBVTT

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.400
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.740
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.330
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:20.830
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.420
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.050
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.640
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.310
by ridding you...

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:43.480
...of your other love?

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.060
At sunset,

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.570
when the children go home,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.490
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.410
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.490
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:04.290
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:09.960
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.800
In a city without light,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.680
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.100
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.350
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.850
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.700
I'm Kurata Sana, a TV personality
with Gekidan Komawari, and 6th grader.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.410
Sagami Rei-kun, my chauffeur
and manager, and former boyfriend,

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:43.040
but we've broken up once and for all.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.330
My Aoki Laureate prize-winning Mama,
and Maro-chan, the chipmunk on her head.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.330
Okay, introduce yourself.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:50.710
I'm the sharp-looking straight-man,
Babbit the white bat.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.840
Hayama Akito. A lot has
happened with him.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:55.670
I don't quite understand the guy.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.010
If Pop dies, what am I going to do?

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.640
Hayama...

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.640
Hayama, be strong.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.980
H- he's all right?

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:11.520
Akito, I'm sorry about this.
Did I startle you?

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.530
Hayama, this is the first time
I've ever seen you

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.400
earnestly concerned for your father.

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:26.290
This Time, Sana is the Lonely Wolf

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:34.300
"Dappi"

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.630
So, in oth-uh woids, "Dappi" is when
you can't poop, even if you really try.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.300
Wait, that's "bempi" (constipation)!

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:39.300
Oh, I wish Zenjiro-san would stop
with the silly poo nonsense already.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:44.310
Ah, we're pushing it, we're pushing it.
We've got a full schedule here...

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:46.970
Does anybody know what
the woid "dappi" means?

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:48.640
Yes!

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:52.980
Yes! Yes! Yes! Zenjiro-sensei!
Me! Me! Pick me! Yes, yes, yes!

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:56.570
--Oh, Sana-chan, you shua
are high-spirited, huh?
--Yes! Yes! Zenjiro-sensei, I know!

00:02:56.570 --> 00:02:59.110
--Awl right... Yoshiko-chan!
--Yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.660
Listen, Zenjiro-chan,
if you don't mind--

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.660
Sana-than, wrap it up, wrap it up.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.660
Yoshiko-chan, you were so close!

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.370
"Dappi" is a little bit different
from the skin that peels awf your body

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.670
aft-uh you get boined
going sea bathing.

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:15.250
Well, I could say it's
quite a bit different.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.670
I oughtta say it's completely different.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.340
Can any of you kids
give me the right answ-uh?

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.010
Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.510
--Wow, Sana-chan, you shua
are en-uh-getic, huh?
--Being energetic is my saving grace!

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.350
Kurata Sana, Shinbo Elementary School,
6th Grade, 3rd Class!

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:28.680
Okay, Uchiyamada.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:34.650
"Dappi" is the extremely
thin, vest-like top

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.650
that you wear during festivals and such.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.940
That's called a "happi"!
Boo on you, Uchiyamada!

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:43.280
Yes! Yes! Yes! Yes!
Everyone, be quiet! Shaddap!

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.950
Let me tell you the right answer,
which I've learned firsthand!

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.910
You're pretty confident, huh?

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.620
In that case, Sana-chan,
let's have your answ-uh.

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:56.380
"Dappi" is when an insect or snake
sheds its old skin. Like this...!

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:01.220
It's also what you call it
when you abandon old ideas

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.630
and flutter your way into a new world.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:07.760
You could say that, too. But is that
costume what you were wearing und-uh--neath?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.640
Everyone, I have to shed
my skin and take off.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.310
Ba-bing, bye-bye, sayonara!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.310
Nice work, everyone.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.690
We're still in the middle of
recording the show, though...

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.030
We've got a commercial shoot
for Hachimitsu Mikanpai up next.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.360
Will we make it in time?

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.990
Yeah, more or less. It's a good thing
you're already wearing your costume.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:27.990
But do bees go through a metamorphosis?

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.620
You can do anything if you
set your mind to it! Whoopee!

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.960
Okay, Sana-chan, fly energetically!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.960
I'm flying! I'm flying energetically!

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.880
Metamorphosis, huh?

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.300
As Sana-chan's manager, I have
to think of her metamorphosis...

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:46.640
Commercials, dramas, singing...

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.350
That's it. Sana-chan is working hard,

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:55.060
and has to shed a skin or two
as an actress to grow.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:59.650
Um, hello? About the commercial...

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:00.980
We'll do it.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.990
It's delicious! Hachimitsu Mikanpai!

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.990
Cut! Right, okay. Sana-chan, good job.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.320
Nicely done!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.660
We're done...

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.330
No, no, we have to do the next one,
the next one!

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.330
The next one? We just finished
the seventh one, right?

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.670
Huh? Didn't I tell you?
I've added three more.

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.330
What!?

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.630
Sana-chan, you were
riding this wave of energy,

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.670
and I thought it would
be wrong to just let it go.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.010
What about dinner? Hey...

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.010
Right, it's waiting for you in the car.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:27.340
Again?

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.600
What choice do I have? Metamorphosis!

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.600
Has eating that curry
turned you into an Indian?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.940
Master Rei, would you please hurry?

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:38.600
Oh, you're in character, huh?

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.940
You betcha! I hail from
Gekidan Komawari, after all!

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.940
Let's go, boss!

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.610
A-yep!

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.780
Way to go, Sana-chan. Stick with it,
even if it's tough.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.160
Good things will happen after
you've stuck it out, I'm sure of it.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.290
Er, probably.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:54.950
Well, there's a chance...

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.290
It'd sure be nice if they did...

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.960
Hey, hey, steady now.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.380
"The Promise"

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.300
Say, Sana-chan,
are you working today, too?

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.630
Mm-hmm, starting this afternoon.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.630
Well, is tomorrow any good?

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.300
Tomorrow? Is something happening?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.640
It's Hisae-chan's birthday party.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.640
Oh, really? Your birthday?

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:15.310
Let's see, I'm on location
at the beach tomorrow, I think.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:17.640
But I should be done by evening,
so can I come after that?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.310
You're going to come?

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:21.650
Uh-huh, I'm coming, I'm coming.
We're best friends, after all, right?

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:24.650
Wow, Hisae-chan,
tomorrow's your birthday?

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:25.990
--Mine's coming up real soon.
--What do you want for a present?

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.320
--It's close, just days away.
--Good question.
--I forgot about that.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:30.660
--It'll be my birthday, too.
--I know what I'm getting her.
--What? What? What?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:31.620
It's a secret.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.620
It's up to you.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.950
--All right. I'll think of
something really good.
--It's soon, days away.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.620
We'll have to think
about what to eat, huh?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:37.620
Sana-chan, what do you like?

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:38.620
Chicken-fried garlic.

00:06:38.620 --> 00:06:39.960
That's so weird!

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:44.630
I wonder if people aren't
taking me too lightly lately.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.300
Did you just laugh at me, Akito-kun?

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:48.630
Not particularly.

00:06:48.630 --> 00:06:51.640
Hmm? What happened to your neck?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.640
I fell.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:53.640
Now?

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.640
It's a secret.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.980
You've always gotten yourself hurt
in the strangest places, haven't you?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.060
That's none of your business, Akito-kun!

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.320
Okay, this is a take! I'd like to
shoot this while it's still daylight,

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:09.320
so let's do our best to that end!

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.660
Right! That's what I'm hoping for!

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.990
All right then, nice and easy!

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:18.000
Sana-chan, run, run!
Faster! Faster! Little more!

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.000
Now stop there! Okay, strike your pose!

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:24.670
I want to be a Kokka Komuin
(government official)!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:27.340
No! This is a juice commercial,
remember?

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:28.670
Ah, that's right.

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:30.680
Let's go again!

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:32.590
Sana-chan, run the way you would!

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.600
That's it, lots of energy!

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:36.260
Now you're doing it like
Kill(ichi Hagimoto)-chan!

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:38.100
And so it went...

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:42.270
When shooting a commercial
with Sana-chan...

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:47.230
...you constantly, constantly, constantly,
constantly have to do re-takes.

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.280
That's not quite right.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.620
It might be too much trouble
for Babbit to hang around with her.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.950
Whew, this is hard.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.280
Okay, smile!

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:58.660
Right!

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.960
Right, that was okay!

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:05.330
Sana-chan, if you like,
take this juice home with you.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.710
Such a hard worker...

00:08:11.970 --> 00:08:15.300
Vita-vita Juice is delicious...
Mm-mm, wrong.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.930
Test it one more time, please...

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.730
This week's Sana-chan.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.980
Edokko Rice Crackers are Japan's best!

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.980
--Whatever... mumble mumble...
--Sagami-kun...

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:29.980
Is she worn out?

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:33.950
I guess shooting commercials for two
weeks straight has been rough on her.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.320
She decided to do them herself.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.620
It's not good for Sana
for you to baby her too much.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:43.960
Hisae-chan, happy birthday...

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.460
Birthday!?

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.920
Morning? Which morning?
What day is it? Who am I?

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.640
Oh, no... Oh, no!

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.140
Yes, Sana-chan crashed like that,

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:04.310
and slept through
Hisae-chan's birthday party.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:07.650
Eh? If I knew, why didn't
I wake her? Tch, tch, tch.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:10.650
A bomb could go off,
and Sana-chan wouldn't wake up.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.820
Right, Sana-chan?

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.650
This is bad! This is bad! This is bad!

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.330
Sure enough...

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:22.950
I'm sorry!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.330
You're awful, Sana-chan!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.620
--She's right, you're awful.
--I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.290
If you couldn't come,
you could have at least called.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.290
I'm sorry.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:34.010
Hisae-chan's mother asked if that girl
who was on TV was going to come,

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.930
and was really looking forward to it.

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.260
I really am sorry.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:40.600
I've had enough of you, Sana-chan.

00:09:40.600 --> 00:09:43.640
What's this, you're fighting?
Have it out.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:49.560
What's going on? What, what?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.940
Sana-chan looks kind of somber.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.240
"Sana, the lonely wolf"

00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:01.950
This is bad. I really blew it. The lunch
tastes good, but this is still bad.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:05.290
You know, I feel a little
sorry for Sana-chan over there.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.620
She said she would come.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.960
Aya-chan, you're too easy on her.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.960
Sana-chan, let's eat together.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:13.300
How come you're being
left out of the group?

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:16.130
--What are you doing, Akito-kun?
Get out of here.
--Yeah, Sana-chan was in the wrong, huh?

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.720
--Leave her be.
--Right, right.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.970
The way girls act is so petty, huh?

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:24.310
What do you mean? You've done
things a lot meaner than them.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:29.150
Yeah, you're right. I wouldn't want
to be known as the number-one mean boy.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.900
Don't go wasting food!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:36.900
What's she doing?
She's not one bit sorry.

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:38.900
Rather, she seems
to be enjoying herself.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:42.410
She's mad! Hisae-chan is mad!
I'm worried.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:48.250
Aw, my thread got tangled again.
I really am clumsy at this, huh?

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:51.630
Clumsy-umsy-umsy,
gonna cut it with scissors...

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:54.920
Better work quietly, huh?

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.090
It's okay. I'll only be busy
for a little while longer.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.300
"A little while longer..."

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:05.350
"Still, it's tough..."

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.270
What?

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:08.930
Sana is depressed?

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.610
Yes. She said she wanted to be
alone until it was time to shoot.

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:16.610
What could be troubling
Japan's most cheerful girl,

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.610
nicknamed "The Fireball Girl,"
Kurata Sana?

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.950
Has she grown despondent of this world?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:25.950
Is she thinking, "Is this the
way I want to live my life?"

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:29.620
Could it be because I've
got her doing too much work?

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:33.630
"Teenage Troubles."
By Kurata Misako. Not bad...

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.300
So, is something wrong with Sana?

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:37.960
Sagami?

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:40.630
Don't tell me this could be
happening to Sana-chan...

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.970
Then again, she is
surprisingly delicate.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:45.720
Sana-chan! I, Sagami Rei,
will protect you,

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:46.640
even if it means my own life!

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.640
Sana-chan!

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.640
♪ A - I - U - E, E- O - A - O,
A - Ka - Sa - Ta - Na... ♪

00:11:49.640 --> 00:11:51.640
♪ A - I - U - E, E - O - A - O,
A - Ka - Sa - Ta - Na... ♪

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:53.650
♪ "That water strider is blue,"
A - I - U - E - O. ♪

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.650
♪ "Persimmon trees, mulberry trees,"
Ka - Ki - Ku - Ke - Ko. ♪

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.650
♪ "Skewer some potluck stew,"
Sa - Shi - Shu - Se - So. ♪

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.650
♪ "Lean some bamboo against a wall,"
Ta - Chi - Tsu - Te - To. ♪

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:01.650
♪ "Uncooked wheat, uncooked rice,"
Na - Ni - Nu - Ne - No. ♪

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.660
♪ "Vocalization practice,"
Ha - Hi - Hu - He - Ho. ♪

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.990
♪ "A magical manteau,"
Ma - Mi - Mu - Me - Mo. ♪

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.990
♪ "Cross the fields, cross the mountains,"
Yodel-ay-hee! ♪

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:10.000
♪ Jungle Tarzan, "Waah-nowaah!" ♪

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.000
♪ Cheetah is with him,
"Oo - kya - kyan - kya!" ♪

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:14.000
♪ Do - Re - Do - Re - Mi -
Re - Do - Re - Adrenaline! ♪

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:16.000
♪ Ba-bing, Bi-bing,
Ba - Bi - Bo - Bu - Be. ♪

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.000
♪ Chan-chan, Bara-bara,
"There's a cloud of dust!" ♪

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:20.340
♪ Boko-boko, "Inside the dust
is a little squirt." ♪

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:22.340
♪ Cheep-cheep, chirp-chirp,
"twitchy little pen." ♪

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.340
♪ "Irritating counterfeit,
I will take my leave." ♪

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:27.680
♪ Shee-shee-shee,
draw a star, clap-clap! ♪

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.020
And with that, my vocalization
practice is down cold.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:32.310
Okay, let's get going to work!

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.560
Right.

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.780
Elegant and revitalizing,
even in the jungle!

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:41.860
Introducing a wild body shampoo!

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.990
Cut! The wind is too strong.
Sana-chan, sorry about that.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:46.990
Okay.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.410
Okay, ready for take 2... Start!

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.330
Elegant and revitalizing,
even in the jungle!

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:58.340
Introducing a wild body shampoo!
This is work, so I have
to make sure I'm smiling.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.090
I have to smile...

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:14.890
You worked really hard, Sana-chan.
That was the last one. We're all done.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.900
All done? Really?

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:19.230
This time, we really are finished.

00:13:19.230 --> 00:13:22.230
All right! Starting tomorrow,
I'm going to play with everyone,

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:22.900
the way I used to!

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:23.900
You bet.

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:25.820
I'll have to make sure to
patch things up with everyone.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:26.910
I'll have to make sure...

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:30.160
Ah... I'm exhausted...

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:42.170
After work, it sure is nice
to have some Japanese tea.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.420
Sana-chan has had it rough.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:49.180
After all, she finished 10 whole
commercials since our last broadcast.

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:52.930
Whew, Babbit has been keeping up
with Sana-chan the whole time,

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.180
and is truly worn out.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.850
You just pop out for a moment,
then withdraw right away, don't you?

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.520
Who are you?

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.770
"Work might be over, but..."

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.530
Huh? What's this?

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.200
Hisae-chan and them
are sending it around.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:12.370
Sana-chan...?

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.580
No, I hate this kind of thing!

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:23.590
"Anyone who talks to Sana-chan
will be ostracized."

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:27.880
Okay, on to page 31.
Here is an interesting problem.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:30.220
Let's open up to it quickly,
solve it right, and finish it up.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.390
Don't be doing anything so stupid!

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:37.890
Never mind.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.200
She's so happy-go-lucky...

00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.870
Say, say, say, say...

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:05.300
Say, say, there was some kind of note
going around, right? Show me. Show me!

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:12.180
Get rid of it.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.680
W- what is this...?

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:24.190
Akito-kun, that was just mean.
This is too mean of them, huh?

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.860
Did you see that note
that was going around?

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.240
I saw, I saw.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:32.160
Looks like those girls are amusing
themselves by shunning Kurata.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.160
Girls sure like to shun people, huh?

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.830
But Kurata is a little
underhanded herself, you know?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:39.830
Taking a nap like that
without getting yelled at.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:43.170
Yeah, that's what I was thinking, too.
That's not fair, huh?

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.170
How about we join in
with their ostracizing?

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:48.510
It has been pretty dull lately.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:51.340
Now that you mention it,
at some point, she was going to--

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.850
Hayama-san...

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:57.390
Do you need the restroom?
Here, go ahead, go ahead.

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:58.850
Go ahead, don't hesitate.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:04.730
I'm... getting angry!

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.070
I sure slept well...

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.870
--There's a fight!
--Where!?

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.540
Sensei, Hayama-kun from 3rd Class
is running wild in the restroom!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:20.200
What?

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:21.540
Tsuyoshi-kun is going crazy, too!

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.040
They're what!?

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:33.800
That's enough, Hayama!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.430
What is the meaning of this, Hayama?

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.640
If you don't tell me,
how am I supposed to know?

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:44.810
Oki?

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.480
You bastards!

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:50.780
All of you, come with me to the staff room!
Geez, what is it with 3rd Class?

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:55.490
What were you guys doing!?

00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:56.780
Dunno.

00:16:58.490 --> 00:17:00.620
"What happened?"

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:22.850
I wonder what the matter with him is.

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:25.850
That wild look in his eyes was back.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.230
"Bothersome."

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:30.860
Are you being shunned by the others?

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:34.490
Aw, it's not all that big a deal!

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:38.160
Is that right? This paper was
going around during class.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:40.950
Hayama and Oki apparently
got angry at the other boys

00:17:40.950 --> 00:17:43.160
because they were
having some fun with it.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:48.170
"Anyone who talks to Sana-chan...
will be ostracized."

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:49.590
Hayama...

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:54.170
Listen, you... What good is it
going to do for you to get mad?

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:58.180
Being the lone wolf is my thing.
It doesn't suit you.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:00.180
You call yourself that?

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:04.850
I couldn't stand to
see you turn into one.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.020
Well, would you not run amuck,

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.270
just because it's something
you couldn't stand?

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:16.190
It's all right. This time,
it really was my fault.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:19.870
Once I offer them another proper apology,
they'll understand.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:23.990
Even so, seeing something like this,
without any warning,

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:26.250
even I might have gotten depressed.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:32.960
But thanks to your wreaking
havoc for me, everything is fine.

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.130
Thanks.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.130
You sure are happy-go-lucky, huh?

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:39.220
Yeah, I really am.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:43.140
Here I am, feeling happy
that you got angry over me.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.470
I'm not that happy about the violence,

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:47.480
but I did get away without
having to be depressed.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.810
I have you to thank for that, Hayama.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:53.820
Nobody said I got angry over you.
I just blew my top, that's all.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.440
That so? Okay, okay...

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:08.000
Hayama, we always seem to be
helping each other out, huh?

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:13.170
We're just half-grown-up kids here,

00:19:13.170 --> 00:19:15.710
so when one of us goes
through some difficulty,

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:17.510
or something we shouldn't be doing,

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.800
as we've fought with each other,
in this short period of time,

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.800
it feels as though we've
started helping each other.

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.350
And up until just a little while ago,
we never even talked to each other,

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.520
you know?

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.690
I'm going to apologize
to everyone again tomorrow.

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:34.440
I'll patch things up right.

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:35.480
Sure you can do that?

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:37.480
It'll be okay, I tell you, Hayama.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:42.660
I'm sure that everyone "doesn't hate me,"
so that's why they got so upset.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:48.500
Don't forget Tsuyoshi, either.
He snapped too, after all.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.790
That's right, Tsuyoshi-kun, too...

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.330
Lately, he's been getting worried

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:53.830
that people aren't paying
as much attention to him.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.960
Mm-hmm. I'll be right back.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.180
Tsuyoshi-kun!

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.390
Huh?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.480
No one cares about me...

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.480
"Pardon me, okay?"

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:16.940
"My bad"

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.400
"Forgive me"

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:22.030
"Sorry"

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:26.530
Say, which one do you think is best?

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:28.540
Such a tough daughter...

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:31.500
That's the thing that's most
Sana-like about Sana-chan, huh?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.290
Maybe I should go
with the direct approach.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:37.460
Yep! Sincerely, sincerely apologize!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:41.130
I really am sorry! I was an idiot!

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.800
Forgive me, I beg you!

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:46.470
You didn't... have to...
apologize so much...

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:49.140
No, I truthfully believe
that it was my fault.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:53.140
Sana-chan, I think that you like
working more than you like us.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:55.810
Naw, I like both, you know?

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:59.150
But I'm done with
my work now, and all.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:00.480
Huh? You're done?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:04.150
Mm-hmm. Yeah, I went boxing
against Zenjiro-san as a kangaroo,

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:06.820
and played Tarzan in the jungle,

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.160
and also played the tragic heroine,
Juliet. "Oh, Romeo..."

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.500
You mean, you did that much work?

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:16.500
Sure, every day, with all the
physical effort, my muscles got so sore!

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:19.500
Then it must have been hard.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:20.500
Just a little.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.840
But it sounds fun! When will they air?

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.510
Most of them will start
coming out next month.

00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:25.840
Wow, I'll check them out!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:27.680
Really? I'm so glad!

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:31.680
"A friendly atmosphere."

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:33.180
What's this?

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:35.850
They're burying the hatchet already?
How boring.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.520
I guess we'll have
to find another target.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.860
Don't do anything stupid.

00:21:40.860 --> 00:21:43.240
I was just joking, Hayama-san.

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:50.200
Um... Hayama-kun...

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:53.540
Tsuyoshi-kun isn't here today.
What could be the matter?

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:56.870
Ah, now that you mention it,
I haven't seen him.

00:21:56.870 --> 00:22:00.210
Tsuyoshi-kun is not the kind of boy
that usually misses class, you know?

00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:04.420
I went to look in his
2nd-grade sister's room too,

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:07.050
but she doesn't appear
to be here, either.

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:16.890
Sensei, have you heard
any word from Tsuyoshi?

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:19.230
Ah, Hayama-kun,
something terrible has happened!

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:20.360
"Terrible?"

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:27.490
Hayama! What is it?
What's wrong? Are you leaving?

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:29.450
It's Tsuyoshi!

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:30.820
Tsuyoshi-kun...?

00:22:30.820 --> 00:22:32.620
Just come with me!

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:35.660
What is it? What is it?

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:42.290
"Back against the wall."

00:22:42.790 --> 00:22:47.800
That's what you say about times like these.

00:22:49.050 --> 00:22:52.550
In dire straits,

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:56.140
I've been waiting for an answer.

00:22:56.640 --> 00:23:00.020
My confessions are worked out
long in advance,

00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:05.110
to always go along with the scenario.

00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:11.110
My heart may be settled, but my mind is in a...

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:13.330
...panic!!

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:19.160
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:21.880
he's there.

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.130
And our usual classroom...

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.710
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:30.220
...for two.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.680
Although I've said nothing but wisecracks...

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:38.430
...up to now, just for today,

00:23:39.350 --> 00:23:42.020
I'm going to be honest and sincere,

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:46.730
so BOY, take a look my way!

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:52.320
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:54.990
he's there,

00:23:55.950 --> 00:23:58.160
And our usual classroom...

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.790
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:24:00.910 --> 00:24:03.290
...for two.

00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:10.340
Hoy! In Sana-chan's next adventures...

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:13.340
Tsuyoshi-kun,
Tsuyoshi-kun, Tsuyoshi-kun...

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:15.680
Whoa, Tsuyoshi-kun, where did you go?

00:24:15.680 --> 00:24:17.680
We went to Tsuyoshi-kun's house and--

00:24:17.680 --> 00:24:20.680
What is the deal with this crazy,
bald old man!? Run!

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:22.600
Of all things,
Tsuyoshi's family has split up.

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:24.600
Oki Tsuyoshi is now Sasaki Tsuyoshi.

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:25.810
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha,

00:24:25.810 --> 00:24:28.940
Episode 13 of the Don't Cry, Strong One,
You're the Oldest Son Saga,

00:24:28.940 --> 00:24:32.610
My Name is Going To Change.

00:24:32.610 --> 00:24:36.030
Square One... Square One... Watch, okay?
